  "worked_solution": "The mode of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that $f(x)$ has a single global maximum at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the mode of $X$ is $2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/72046f8f852b5fc53226fa611718011f2f8b58ee0672bfd8862ad506548156cb.png)",
